<SiteLayout
  title="Contact — Action Models for Robot Learning"
  description="How to reach Pavan Kumar Kandapagari about the open-access textbook Action Models for Robot Learning."
  currentPath="contact"
>
  <main class="toc-page">
    <h1>Get in touch</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      Reader notes are the most useful input this book gets.
    </p>

    <p>
      A typo, a spot where the argument goes unclear, a section that doesn't deliver on what its
      title promised, a reference I should have cited: all of it lands well. I read everything.
      Replies are best-effort and can take a few days, so pick whichever channel below matches
      what you want to say.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>GitHub</strong> —
      <a href="https://github.com/kandapagari/in-action-book">github.com/kandapagari/in-action-book</a>.
      The natural home for typo fixes, draft feedback, open issues, and pull
      requests on the manuscript. Anything worth discussing in public belongs
      here.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Email</strong> —
      <a href="mailto:pavan.kandapagari@gmail.com">pavan.kandapagari@gmail.com</a>.
      Better for collaboration, longer questions, and anything that doesn't fit
      a public issue.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>LinkedIn</strong> —
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kandapagari/">linkedin.com/in/kandapagari</a>.
      Fine for professional introductions, talks, and conference invitations.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Personal site</strong> —
      <a href="https://kandapagari.vercel.app">kandapagari.vercel.app</a>.
      Broader notes and projects outside this book.
    </p>

    <p>
      The book stays open-access, and the manuscript lives in public on GitHub. Contributions of
      any size are welcome: a single typo, a clearer figure caption, or a full rewrite of a
      section. See <a href="/about/">the about page</a> for what the book is and how I'm writing
      it.
    </p>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
